 </blockquote>
 <p>After obtaining the AUC scores, you can go directly to “Step 2” and “Follow up examples”. However, you can keep reading through section 1.1 and 1.2 if you want to understand better what these scores mean, or if you would like to run AUCell across many gene-sets that need further manipulation.</p>
 <p>In brief, the AUC scores are calculated in two steps: 1. Building the rankings (<code>AUCell_buildRankings</code>) and 2. Calculate enrichment (<code>AUCell_calcAUC</code>). i.e. using <code>AUCell_run</code> is equivalent to running:</p>
-<pre class="r"><code>cells_rankings &lt;- AUCell_buildRankings(exprMatrix, plotStats=FALSE, splitByBlocks=TRUE)
